{"openapi":"3.1.0","info":{"title":"Memchats API","version":"1.0.0","description":"REST API for the Memchats conversation memory and for Alma, the single counsellor who answers about a contact. Alma covers four areas (legal, relaciones, conocer, negocio) and picks one from who the contact is and what the exchange is about. No area depends on the plan: all four are available on every plan, Free included. Plans differ in how many Alma analyses per week they allow, how many contacts can be kept, and how deep the answer goes.","contact":{"url":"https://memchats.com/developers"}},"servers":[{"url":"https://memchats.com"}],"security":[{"bearerAuth":[]}],"components":{"securitySchemes":{"bearerAuth":{"type":"http","scheme":"bearer","description":"API key starting with mc_live_. Generate at /ajustes/api-keys."}},"schemas":{"DatingProfile":{"type":"object","nullable":true,"properties":{"network":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"originNetwork":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"nickname":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"age":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"distanceKm":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"location":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"residency":{"type":"string","enum":["local","visiting","unknown"]},"contentLanguage":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"uiLanguage":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"languages":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"lookingFor":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"casual, serious, friendship or unclear."},"hasKids":{"type":"boolean","nullable":true},"wantsKids":{"type":"boolean","nullable":true},"ageRangeSought":{"type":"object","nullable":true,"properties":{"min":{"type":"integer"},"max":{"type":"integer"}}},"bio":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"bioLanguage":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"ISO 639-1 of the bio: detected on the text, else contentLanguage."},"interests":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"photoHooks":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"updatedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","nullable":true}}},"DatingDiscrepancy":{"type":"object","properties":{"field":{"type":"string"},"profileValue":{},"chatValue":{},"message":{"type":"string","description":"Spanish sentence to show as is."}}},"DatingPhoto":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"integer"},"position":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"hasFace":{"type":"boolean","nullable":true},"caption":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"width":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"height":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"source":{"type":"string","enum":["auto","manual"],"description":"`manual` when the user cropped it by hand from a screenshot."},"screenshotId":{"type":"integer","nullable":true,"description":"The original screenshot it came from (GET /contact-screenshots/{screenshotId}/image); null for photos saved before 2026-10-05."},"isCover":{"type":"boolean","description":"The cover the user chose: after a reorder, the first photo."}}},"DatingNetworkPeriod":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"integer"},"network":{"type":"string"},"startedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date"},"endedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date","nullable":true},"note":{"type":"string","nullable":true}}},"DatingSuggestion":{"type":"object","description":"The latest message proposal saved for this contact (the import wizard, or the last suggest-message). `null` when none was ever generated.","properties":{"text":{"type":"string"},"intent":{"type":"string","enum":["open","reply","revive","propose_date"]},"charLimit":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"rationale":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"language":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"variants":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DatingSuggestionVariants"},"createdAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"}}},"DatingSuggestionVariants":{"type":"array","nullable":true,"description":"2 or 3 drafts of distinct tone written in the same model call (2026-10-05), each within `charLimit`; the first one equals `text`. Absent or null when the model gave only one.","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string"},"tone":{"type":"string","enum":["direct","playful","curious"]}}}},"DatingProposalTurn":{"type":"object","description":"Whose turn it is for the next proposal (2026-10-05). `write` with the intent to use (open without messages; reply, or propose_date when she put a live date on the table, after her message; revive after his own message 48 h or more ago). `wait`: his message is the last one and it is too soon to write again; `reviveAfter` says from when. Hours and `reviveAfter` are null when the screenshots showed no time.","properties":{"action":{"type":"string","enum":["write","wait"]},"intent":{"type":"string","enum":["open","reply","revive","propose_date"],"description":"Only with `write`."},"hoursSinceLastMessage":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"reviveAfter":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","nullable":true,"description":"Only with `wait`."}}},"DatingConversationState":{"type":"object","properties":{"whoseTurn":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"me, her or null."},"lastMessageFrom":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"me, her or null."},"sheAskedQuestion":{"type":"boolean"},"daysSinceLastMessage":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"urgency":{"type":"string","enum":["owes_answer","owes_reply","waiting_on_her","needs_new_reason","fresh"]},"urgencyMessage":{"type":"string","description":"Spanish sentence to show as is."},"herMedianReplyHours":{"type":"number","nullable":true,"description":"null with fewer than two replies measured on times seen in the screenshots."},"herReplySamples":{"type":"integer"},"lastMessageAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","nullable":true},"lastMessageTimeKnown":{"type":"boolean","description":"false when the time was not visible in the imported screenshots: lastMessageAt is then the import time and daysSinceLastMessage is null."},"herLastMessageAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","nullable":true},"lastReplyDelayHours":{"type":"number","nullable":true},"reactionSignal":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"faster_than_usual, normal, slower_than_usual or null."},"deferrals":{"type":"integer"}}},"DatingRow":{"type":"object","properties":{"contactId":{"type":"integer"},"conversationId":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"name":{"type":"string"},"nickname":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"network":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"originNetwork":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"age":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"distanceKm":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"residency":{"type":"string","enum":["local","visiting","unknown"]},"lastMessageAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","nullable":true},"herLastReplyAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","nullable":true},"whoseTurn":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"me, her or null."},"sheAskedQuestion":{"type":"boolean"},"daysSinceLastMessage":{"type":"number","nullable":true,"description":"One decimal."},"urgency":{"type":"string","enum":["owes_answer","owes_reply","waiting_on_her","needs_new_reason","fresh"]},"urgencyMessage":{"type":"string","description":"Spanish sentence to show as is."},"reactionSignal":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"description":"faster_than_usual, normal, slower_than_usual or null."},"hasProfile":{"type":"boolean"},"coverPhotoId":{"type":"integer","nullable":true,"description":"First photo with a face by position (falls back to the first photo), for the avatar."},"createdAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","nullable":true}}},"PeopleImportStatus":{"type":"object","description":"What the people import client polls. Small on purpose: one Redis read per poll.","required":["importId","status","images"],"properties":{"importId":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["processing","needs_name","done","failed"]},"phase":{"type":"string","enum":["reading","saving","suggesting"],"description":"Only while processing: reading the screenshots, saving the person and the chat, or preparing the first proposal. Absent on servers before 2026-10-03."},"images":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"index":{"type":"integer"},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["pending","processing","done","failed"]},"class":{"type":"string","enum":["dating_profile","chat","other"],"description":"What the image turned out to be, once read."}}}},"nameCandidates":{"type":"array","description":"Present from needs_name on: the chips of \"¿Cómo se llama?\". Empty when no name was visible.","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"source":{"type":"string","enum":["chat_header","profile_name","signature","mention"]},"confidence":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":1}}}},"result":{"type":"object","description":"Present when status is done.","properties":{"contactId":{"type":"integer"},"conversationId":{"type":"integer","nullable":true,"description":"Null for a dating import without chat screenshots."},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["dating","conversation"]},"target":{"type":"string","enum":["dating","conversation"],"description":"The screen to land on."},"contactName":{"type":"string"},"relationshipType":{"type":"string"},"inserted":{"type":"integer"},"suggestionStatus":{"type":"string","enum":["generated","pending","skipped_demo_limit","skipped_quota","skipped_no_content","skipped_her_turn","failed"],"description":"`pending`: the proposal outlived the wait of the processing screen and is still being written; it lands in the contact's Alma thread (conversation) or on GET /contacts/{id}/dating (dating) when done, and the stored status is updated. `failed` only means the generation failed. `skipped_her_turn` (dating): his message is the last one and it is too soon to write again; nothing was generated or spent, see `herTurn`."},"herTurn":{"type":"object","description":"Only with `skipped_her_turn`. Both null when the screenshots showed no time (no hours are invented).","properties":{"hoursSinceLastMessage":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"reviveAfter":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","nullable":true}}},"suggestion":{"type":"object","description":"The first proposal, already generated. dating: {kind, text, intent (open|reply|revive|propose_date, decided by whose turn it is), charLimit, situation, rationale, language, variants?} where `variants` are 2 or 3 drafts of distinct tone ({text, tone: direct|playful|curious}) from the same call, the first equal to `text`. conversation: {kind, entryId, title, body, suggestedReply}, stored as an entry of the contact's Alma thread."}}},"error":{"type":"object","properties":{"code":{"type":"string"},"message":{"type":"string"}}}}},"ImportingStatus":{"type":"object","nullable":true,"description":"Non-null while the initial memory sweep of this contact is running. `phase` alternates between reading a stretch of conversation and filing what was found in it; a pass is about a minute, which is why both are published.","properties":{"processed":{"type":"integer","description":"Messages read so far."},"total":{"type":"integer","description":"Messages this sweep will read."},"passIndex":{"type":"integer"},"passCount":{"type":"integer"},"phase":{"type":"string","enum":["reading","writing"]},"passRange":{"type":"object","nullable":true,"description":"The stretch of conversation the current pass covers.","properties":{"fromMessageId":{"type":"integer"},"toMessageId":{"type":"integer"},"fromAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"toAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"messages":{"type":"integer"}}},"startedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"updatedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"Last heartbeat. `startedAt` alone cannot tell a sweep that is working from one whose worker died."}}}}},"paths":{"/api/v1/contacts/{id}":{"get":{"summary":"Read a contact","description":"Who this person is to the user, the note kept about them, and `reimportSuggested`: three weeks without a new message on a contact whose history has already been read once.","operationId":"getContact","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The contact row, the reimport nudge, and `importing`: the live sweep of this contact or null. While it is not null the memory of this contact is still being built.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"integer"},"name":{"type":"string"},"display_name":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"relationship_type":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"context_note":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"created_at":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","nullable":true},"reimportSuggested":{"type":"boolean"},"importing":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ImportingStatus"}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Not found"}}},"patch":{"summary":"Rename a contact or change the note kept about them","description":"Only `displayName` and `contextNote`. Changing who the person is to the user goes through /relationship, because that closes one period and opens another.","operationId":"updateContact","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Updated"},"400":{"description":"Nothing to update, or a value out of range"},"404":{"description":"Not found"}}},"delete":{"summary":"Delete a contact and everything attached to it","description":"Irreversible. Removes the contact, its conversations, messages, memory and stored documents.","operationId":"deleteContact","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Deleted"},"404":{"description":"Not found"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/dating-profile":{"get":{"summary":"Read the dating profile built from this contact's screenshots","description":"Null when no screenshot has been analysed yet, which is a normal state rather than an error.","operationId":"getDatingProfile","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The profile, or null","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"profile":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DatingProfile"}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Contact not found"}}},"post":{"summary":"Analyse a dating-app screenshot and merge it into the profile","description":"Costs a vision model call. Reads the screenshot with a vision model and extracts structured fields: network, nickname, age, distance, whether she lives there or is passing through, the two languages (app UI vs what she wrote), what she is looking for, kids, her verbatim bio, interests and concrete hooks from her photos. A newer screenshot is MERGED into the stored profile: an empty or unknown value never overwrites a known one, and when a chat screenshot contradicts the profile on location, residency, age or what she is looking for, the chat wins and the contradiction is returned in `discrepancies`. `originNetwork` is only set the first time. The first time a network is known, a network history period is opened. A contact whose relationship is not in the dating family is switched to `dating`. Returns `screenshotKind`, which decides whether the next message has a character limit.","operationId":"analyseDatingScreenshot","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"multipart/form-data":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"file":{"type":"string","format":"binary"},"screenshot":{"type":"string","format":"binary","description":"Legacy name for `file`."}},"required":["file"]}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The merged profile, the contradictions found and screenshotKind","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"profile":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DatingProfile"},"discrepancies":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DatingDiscrepancy"}},"screenshotKind":{"type":"string","enum":["profile","chat","profile_and_chat"]}}}}}},"400":{"description":"No screenshot in the request, or an unknown network"},"404":{"description":"Contact not found"},"413":{"description":"Over 15 MB"},"415":{"description":"Not an accepted image type"},"422":{"description":"The screenshot could not be read"}}},"patch":{"summary":"Correct a field the model read wrong","description":"Only the fields worth fixing by hand: network, originNetwork, nickname, age, distanceKm, residency and lookingFor (the snake_case spellings are still accepted). Everything else is re-extracted by uploading another screenshot. Moving the conversation to another network is PUT /dating-network, which keeps the history.","operationId":"updateDatingProfile","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Updated"},"400":{"description":"Nothing to change, or a value out of range"},"404":{"description":"No dating profile for this contact yet"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/suggest-message":{"post":{"summary":"Draft a message for a dating conversation","description":"Costs a model call. Combines her profile with the user's voice profile. First contact is capped at 140 characters (the Tinder limit); an open conversation removes the cap. Without `history` (or with an empty one) the server uses the last 40 stored messages of this contact. With `correction` (\"Muy light\", \"Más corto\"...) the correction is appended to the dating voice profile exactly as POST /voice-profile does (creating the profile from the default voice when there is none) and the draft is regenerated obeying it. Requires a dating profile: without one, a personalised message is a generic line with her name in it.","operationId":"suggestDatingMessage","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"intent":{"type":"string","enum":["open","reply","revive","propose_date"],"default":"open"},"charLimitOverride":{"type":"integer","minimum":20,"maximum":2000,"nullable":true},"history":{"type":"array","maxItems":50,"items":{"type":"object","properties":{"from":{"type":"string","enum":["me","her"]},"text":{"type":"string"}},"required":["from","text"]}},"correction":{"type":"string","maxLength":500,"nullable":true}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The draft, the situation, open plans, the language chosen, the limit applied and why","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"suggestion":{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string"},"situation":{"type":"string"},"openPlans":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"language":{"type":"string"},"charLimit":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"rationale":{"type":"string"},"variants":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DatingSuggestionVariants"}}}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid request"},"404":{"description":"Contact not found"},"409":{"description":"No dating profile for this contact yet"}}}},"/api/v1/dating":{"get":{"summary":"List dating conversations, sorted by what can be acted on","description":"The only list where dating contacts appear (relationship family dating, or with a dating profile). Each row carries whose turn it is, how long the conversation has been still and the urgency computed from the last 200 messages. `coolingCount` counts the rows where it is the user's turn and the conversation has been still for 2 days or more.","operationId":"listDating","parameters":[{"name":"sort","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"string","enum":["recent","oldest","network","stale","her_silence","my_turn"],"default":"my_turn"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The rows, already sorted","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"rows":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DatingRow"}},"coolingCount":{"type":"integer"},"sort":{"type":"string"},"quota":{"type":"object","description":"This month's dating usage against the plan (Madrid calendar month). `limit` null means no ceiling.","properties":{"images":{"type":"object","properties":{"used":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer","nullable":true}}},"suggestions":{"type":"object","properties":{"used":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer","nullable":true}}},"resetsAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"}}}}}}}}}}},"/api/v1/dating/own-profile":{"get":{"summary":"The latest analysis of the user's OWN dating profile and bio","description":"FlirtMaster edition only: in the Memchats edition it answers 404 with `code: \"edition_feature_unavailable\"`. Returns the last photo analysis and the last bio analysis stored for this user (either can be null), so a screen can show them again without another model call.","operationId":"getOwnDatingProfileReview","responses":{"200":{"description":"`{ review: { photoAnalysis, photoAnalyzedAt, screenshotCount, bioAnalysis, bioAnalyzedAt } }`"},"404":{"description":"Not part of this edition (`edition_feature_unavailable`)"}}}},"/api/v1/dating/own-profile/analysis":{"post":{"summary":"Analyse screenshots of the user's OWN dating profile","description":"Costs a vision model call. FlirtMaster edition only (404 `edition_feature_unavailable` otherwise). Multipart with 1 to 10 screenshots in `files` (png, jpeg, webp, heic; 15 MB each, 40 MB in total). Returns the detected network, a per-photo assessment (what it communicates and its quality issues), the recommended photo order and why the first one, photos to drop, missing photo types, prompt answers judged, the literal bio if visible and the top 3 changes by expected impact. It talks about photos, never about how the person looks. Limited to 10 per user and hour; a demo session spends from the same 5-generation cap as suggest-message and nothing is stored.","operationId":"analyzeOwnDatingProfile","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"multipart/form-data":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"files":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","format":"binary"},"minItems":1,"maxItems":10}},"required":["files"]}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"`{ analysis, screenshotCount }`"},"400":{"description":"No screenshots, or more than 10"},"404":{"description":"Not part of this edition (`edition_feature_unavailable`)"},"413":{"description":"A screenshot over 15 MB, or over 40 MB in total"},"415":{"description":"Unsupported image format"},"422":{"description":"The screenshots could not be analysed"},"429":{"description":"Hourly limit, the demo cap (`demo_suggestion_limit`), or the Monthly own-profile analyses of the plan (`own_profile_quota_exceeded`, with `limit`, `used`, `remaining`, `resetsAt`; Free 6, Plus 20, Pro and Empresa 40, shared by the analysis and bio routes; admins and demo sessions are not held to it)"}}}},"/api/v1/dating/own-profile/bio":{"post":{"summary":"Critique the user's OWN dating bio and rewrite it three times in their voice","description":"Costs a model call. FlirtMaster edition only (404 `edition_feature_unavailable` otherwise). Without `bio`, the one read from the last screenshot analysis is used (400 `bio_missing` if there is none). `network` sets the character limit every rewrite is fitted to (default: the network of the last analysis, else tinder). `languages` are ISO 639-1 codes, up to 3; each rewrite comes in every requested language. Uses the dating voice profile when there is one. Limited to 20 per user and hour; a demo session spends from the same 5-generation cap as suggest-message and nothing is stored.","operationId":"analyzeOwnDatingBio","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"bio":{"type":"string","maxLength":3000,"nullable":true},"network":{"type":"string","enum":["tinder","bumble","badoo","hinge","facebook","instagram","whatsapp","telegram","parejas","other"],"nullable":true},"languages":{"type":"array","maxItems":3,"items":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[a-zA-Z]{2}$"}}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"`{ analysis: { network, charLimit, languages, critique, rewrites, usedVoiceProfile } }`"},"400":{"description":"Invalid body, or no bio to analyse (`bio_missing`)"},"404":{"description":"Not part of this edition (`edition_feature_unavailable`)"},"422":{"description":"The bio could not be analysed"},"429":{"description":"Hourly limit, the demo cap (`demo_suggestion_limit`), or the Monthly own-profile analyses of the plan (`own_profile_quota_exceeded`, with `limit`, `used`, `remaining`, `resetsAt`; Free 6, Plus 20, Pro and Empresa 40, shared by the analysis and bio routes; admins and demo sessions are not held to it)"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/dating":{"get":{"summary":"Everything the dating detail screen needs, in one call","description":"The contact, the dating profile, the conversation state (whose turn, urgency and the sentence to show), the photos, the network history and the profile/chat discrepancies. Discrepancies are only computed when a screenshot is merged (POST /dating-profile) and are not stored, so this list is currently always empty.","operationId":"getDatingDetail","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The aggregate","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"contact":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"integer"},"name":{"type":"string"},"conversationId":{"type":"integer","nullable":true}}},"profile":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DatingProfile"},"state":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DatingConversationState"},"photos":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DatingPhoto"}},"networkHistory":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DatingNetworkPeriod"}},"discrepancies":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DatingDiscrepancy"}},"suggestion":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DatingSuggestion"},"turn":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DatingProposalTurn"},"recentMessages":{"type":"array","description":"The last messages of either side, oldest first, with the language of each text.","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"integer"},"from":{"type":"string","enum":["me","her"]},"text":{"type":"string"},"sentAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"timeKnown":{"type":"boolean","description":"false: sentAt is the import time, not the message time."},"language":{"type":"string","nullable":true}}}}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Contact not found"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/translate":{"post":{"summary":"Translate stored texts of a dating contact","description":"By reference only: her bio, stored messages of this contact (by id) or the saved proposal; free text is not accepted. Cached per contact, text and target language: a text already translated costs no model call, and the limits (30 model calls per hour, a daily cap per plan, the demo's shared generation slots) are only spent on a model call.","operationId":"translateDatingTexts","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","required":["target","items"],"properties":{"target":{"type":"string","enum":["es","en","fr","de","it","pt"]},"items":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":20,"items":{"type":"object","required":["kind"],"properties":{"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["bio","message","suggestion"]},"id":{"type":"integer","description":"Message id, only for kind=message."},"variant":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":2,"description":"Only for kind=suggestion: which of the saved proposal's variants to translate (default 0, the first)."}}}}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"One translation per item","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"target":{"type":"string"},"translations":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["bio","message","suggestion"]},"id":{"type":"integer"},"sourceLanguage":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"text":{"type":"string"},"cached":{"type":"boolean"}}}}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid request (unsupported target, free text, too many items)"},"404":{"description":"Contact not found, or an item that does not belong to it"},"429":{"description":"rate_limited, translation_quota or demo_suggestion_limit (see code), with retry-after"},"502":{"description":"The model returned nothing usable"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/dating-network":{"put":{"summary":"Move a dating conversation to another network","description":"Closes the open network period (endedAt = today), opens a new one and updates the profile network. Conversations move from Tinder to Instagram to WhatsApp and each jump is kept. Sending the network that is already open changes nothing.","operationId":"setDatingNetwork","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","required":["network"],"properties":{"network":{"type":"string","enum":["tinder","bumble","badoo","hinge","facebook","instagram","whatsapp","telegram","parejas","other"]},"note":{"type":"string","maxLength":500}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The full network history and the profile","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"networkHistory":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DatingNetworkPeriod"}},"profile":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DatingProfile"}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Unknown network or invalid body"},"404":{"description":"Contact not found"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/dating-photos":{"get":{"summary":"List the photos cropped from this person's screenshots","description":"Ordered by their position in the profile. The image itself is served by GET /dating-photos/{photoId}/image; there are no public or presigned URLs, because these are photos of third parties.","operationId":"listDatingPhotos","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The photo rows"},"404":{"description":"Contact not found"}}},"post":{"summary":"Crop the photos out of a profile screenshot into the gallery","description":"Costs a vision model call (skipped when the gallery is already full). Crops each photo without the app chrome on top and stores it, so the person can be remembered after the profile disappears. A photo already in the gallery is not added again, positions continue after the last photo, and a contact keeps at most 12 photos; `skippedDuplicates` and `skippedOverLimit` say what was left out.","operationId":"addDatingPhotos","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"multipart/form-data":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"file":{"type":"string","format":"binary"},"screenshot":{"type":"string","format":"binary","description":"Legacy name for `file`."},"network":{"type":"string","enum":["tinder","bumble","badoo","hinge","facebook","instagram","whatsapp","telegram","parejas","other"]}},"required":["file"]}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The photos added (empty with a note when none was found)"},"400":{"description":"No screenshot in the request, or an unknown network"},"404":{"description":"Contact not found"},"413":{"description":"Over 15 MB"},"415":{"description":"Not an accepted image type"},"422":{"description":"The screenshot could not be read"},"500":{"description":"The crops could not be saved (nothing is left in storage)"},"503":{"description":"Image storage not configured"}}},"patch":{"summary":"Reorder the gallery of this person; the first photo becomes the cover","description":"`order` must list the ids of ALL the photos of this contact, each once, in the new order; otherwise 400 `photo_order_mismatch` and nothing changes (the gallery changed elsewhere: reload it). Positions are rewritten 0..n-1 in one transaction and the first photo is marked `isCover`. Rejected for demo sessions.","operationId":"reorderDatingPhotos","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"order":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"integer"},"minItems":1,"maxItems":12}},"required":["order"]}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The photos in their new order","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"photos":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DatingPhoto"}}}}}}},"400":{"description":"`invalid_order` (not a list of ids) or `photo_order_mismatch` (not exactly the photos of this contact)"},"401":{"description":"No session"},"403":{"description":"Demo session (read only)"},"404":{"description":"Contact not found"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/dating-photos/crop":{"post":{"summary":"Crop a photo by hand out of one original screenshot of this person","description":"For when the automatic crop failed. `rect` is in fractions 0-1 of the screenshot as shown (EXIF orientation applied), at least 0.05 on each side and inside the image. The stored original is cropped (no model call, no quota), encoded like every other gallery photo, and appended at the end with `source: manual` and its `screenshotId`. The same rules as the automatic crop apply: a photo already in the gallery is not added twice and a contact keeps at most 12. Errors carry a stable `code`. Rejected for demo sessions.","operationId":"cropDatingPhoto","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"screenshotId":{"type":"integer","description":"A screenshot of this contact (the `screenshots` block of GET /contacts/{id}/dating)."},"rect":{"type":"object","properties":{"x":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":1},"y":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":1},"w":{"type":"number","minimum":0.05,"maximum":1},"h":{"type":"number","minimum":0.05,"maximum":1}},"required":["x","y","w","h"]}},"required":["screenshotId","rect"]}}}},"responses":{"201":{"description":"The photo added","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"photo":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/DatingPhoto"}}}}}},"400":{"description":"`invalid_rect`: missing screenshot id, or a rectangle outside the image or too small"},"401":{"description":"No session"},"403":{"description":"Demo session (read only)"},"404":{"description":"Contact not found, `screenshot_not_found` (not of this contact or user) or `screenshot_unreadable`"},"409":{"description":"`gallery_full` (12 photos) or `duplicate_photo` (already in the gallery)"},"422":{"description":"`crop_too_small`: under 48 px on a side of the original"},"429":{"description":"Too many uploads or crops in a short time"},"503":{"description":"`storage_unavailable`: image storage not configured"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/dating-photos/{photoId}":{"delete":{"summary":"Delete one photo from the gallery of this person","description":"Removes the row and its stored image (unless another row still cites the same object). 404 both when it does not exist and when it belongs to another account or another contact.","operationId":"deleteDatingPhoto","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}},{"name":"photoId","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Deleted"},"400":{"description":"Invalid id"},"401":{"description":"No session"},"403":{"description":"Demo session (read only)"},"404":{"description":"Photo not found"}}}},"/api/v1/contact-screenshots/{screenshotId}/image":{"get":{"summary":"The image of one original screenshot of a person","description":"Every screenshot uploaded of a person (profile and chat) is kept and listed in the `screenshots` block of GET /contacts/{id}/dating. Streams the image after checking that it belongs to the caller. `Cache-Control: private`. 404 both when it does not exist and when it belongs to someone else.","operationId":"getContactScreenshotImage","parameters":[{"name":"screenshotId","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The image","content":{"image/*":{"schema":{"type":"string","format":"binary"}}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid id"},"404":{"description":"Screenshot not found"},"503":{"description":"Image storage not configured"}}}},"/api/v1/dating-photos/{photoId}/image":{"get":{"summary":"The image of one dating photo","description":"Streams the JPEG after checking that the photo belongs to the caller. `Cache-Control: private, max-age=3600`. 404 both when it does not exist and when it belongs to someone else.","operationId":"getDatingPhotoImage","parameters":[{"name":"photoId","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The image","content":{"image/jpeg":{"schema":{"type":"string","format":"binary"}}}},"404":{"description":"Photo not found"},"503":{"description":"Image storage not configured"}}}},"/api/v1/voice-profile":{"get":{"summary":"Read how the user writes, per area","description":"Areas keep their own voice: nobody writes to a date the way they write to a client. Null when unset, which is a normal state.","operationId":"getVoiceProfile","parameters":[{"name":"area","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"string"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The profile, or null"}}},"put":{"summary":"Set how the user writes","description":"Upserts by (user, area) so editing never loses the accumulated corrections, which are the most valuable thing stored here.","operationId":"setVoiceProfile","responses":{"200":{"description":"Saved"},"400":{"description":"Invalid request"}}},"post":{"summary":"Record a correction to a drafted message","description":"Its own verb rather than a field on PUT, because a correction (\"too light\", \"too long\") describes the user more precisely than any form they could fill in. Keeps the twelve most recent: style shifts, and a correction from months ago may contradict what they want today.","operationId":"addVoiceCorrection","responses":{"200":{"description":"Recorded"},"400":{"description":"Invalid request"},"404":{"description":"No voice profile to correct yet"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/patterns/{patternId}/dismiss":{"post":{"summary":"Put a detected pattern away","description":"Detection runs on its own after every ingest, so this is how a false positive stops being shown. `reason` is optional and stored when given. The contact in the path is checked as well as the owner: a pattern id alone does not say which conversation it belongs to.","operationId":"dismissContactPattern","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}},{"name":"patternId","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"requestBody":{"required":false,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"reason":{"type":"string","maxLength":500}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The pattern, now dismissed"},"400":{"description":"Malformed ids, body, or a reason over 500 characters"},"404":{"description":"No such pattern on this contact"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/relationship":{"get":{"summary":"Every period this contact has been through","description":"The relationship is dated: partner from 2019, ex-partner from 14/03/2026. The current period is the one with a null `ended_at`.","operationId":"getContactRelationship","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"History, oldest first, plus the current period"}}},"post":{"summary":"Record that the contact is now something else to the user","description":"Closes the open period on `startedAt` and opens a new one, and asks for the memory sheet to be read again in the new light.","operationId":"setContactRelationship","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The new period and the full history"},"400":{"description":"Unknown relationship type or malformed date"},"404":{"description":"Not found"}}}},"/api/v1/alma/respond":{"get":{"summary":"List previous Alma entries","description":"Optional `proposalInProgress` (boolean): `true` while the first Alma proposal of a people import for this contact is still being written, `false` once it has ended (stored or failed). Clients waiting for that proposal keep polling while it is `true`. Absent when the server cannot tell; clients then use their own fixed wait.","operationId":"listAlmaEntries","parameters":[{"name":"contactId","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"`{ entries, proposalInProgress? }`: the thread, oldest first, and whether an import proposal is still being written"}}},"post":{"summary":"Ask Alma about a contact","description":"Consumes one LLM query from the weekly plan quota. Alma picks the area (legal, relaciones, conocer, negocio) from who the contact is and what the exchange is about; no area depends on the plan.","operationId":"almaRespond","responses":{"200":{"description":"Answer, with the citations it is based on"},"429":{"description":"Weekly Alma analysis quota exhausted, with `resetsAt`"}}}},"/api/v1/alma/briefing":{"post":{"summary":"Make sure a contact has Alma's initial briefing","description":"Written once per contact, when the memory sweep finishes. This endpoint is the safety net for contacts imported before briefings existed, and for sweeps where that call failed. It does NOT consume the weekly Alma quota: nobody asked a question. It cannot be used to spend either, because at most one briefing entry exists per contact (a partial unique index), and a caller that does not claim that slot never reaches the model. `building` means the contact's memory is not ready yet, which is the honest answer rather than a briefing about an empty sheet.","operationId":"ensureAlmaBriefing","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","required":["contactId"],"properties":{"contactId":{"type":"integer"}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"`{ status: 'ready', entry }` with the briefing, or `{ status: 'building' }` while the memory is still being built"},"404":{"description":"No such contact for this account"},"503":{"description":"`{ status: 'unavailable' }`: the model could not write it; it is retried on the next open"}}}},"/api/v1/alma/entries/{id}/feedback":{"post":{"summary":"Say what you did with a suggested reply","description":"`accepted` when you will send it, `rejected` when you would rather say something else, with an optional one-line reason. Answering twice returns 409: the first verdict stands.","operationId":"setSuggestionFeedback","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The stored verdict"},"400":{"description":"Unknown status or a reason over 500 characters"},"404":{"description":"Not found"},"409":{"description":"Already answered"}}}},"/api/v1/alma/insights":{"get":{"summary":"Cross-contact insights","operationId":"getAlmaInsights","responses":{"200":{"description":"Insights with the evidence behind them"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/documents":{"get":{"summary":"List documents attached to a contact","operationId":"listContactDocuments","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Documents with their processing status"}}},"post":{"summary":"Attach a document to a contact","description":"multipart/form-data. The original is stored in object storage.","operationId":"uploadContactDocument","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Stored, queued for text extraction"},"413":{"description":"File too large"},"415":{"description":"Unsupported type"},"503":{"description":"Document storage unavailable"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/documents/{docId}":{"get":{"summary":"Get a document, or the file itself with ?raw=1","operationId":"getContactDocument","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}},{"name":"docId","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}},{"name":"raw","in":"query","schema":{"type":"integer","enum":[1]}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Document metadata, or the file when raw=1"}}}},"/api/v1/connections":{"get":{"summary":"List the user's connections to MemoryFirst and TubExperto","description":"The stored API key is never returned: only its last four characters, in `secretHint`. `available` is false when the server has no CONNECTIONS_SECRET_KEY, so connections cannot be stored or used. `usage` carries `{ used, limit }` for a provider with a monthly cap (TubExperto, whose key is the user's own and spends their credits) and is null for one without (MemoryFirst).","operationId":"listConnections","responses":{"200":{"description":"Connections, without secrets"},"403":{"description":"Connections require the Pro or Empresa plan"}}},"post":{"summary":"Store (or replace) the connection to one provider","description":"One connection per provider and user: posting again rotates the key. The secret is encrypted at rest with AES-256-GCM and never returned.","operationId":"createConnection","responses":{"201":{"description":"Stored; only the hint comes back"},"403":{"description":"Connections require the Pro or Empresa plan"},"422":{"description":"Unknown provider, secret too short, or a non-https base URL"},"503":{"description":"The server has no CONNECTIONS_SECRET_KEY"}}},"delete":{"summary":"Remove a connection","operationId":"deleteConnection","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Removed"},"400":{"description":"Missing or malformed id"},"404":{"description":"Not found"}}}},"/api/v1/connections/{id}/test":{"post":{"summary":"Check a connection against its provider","description":"Sends the cheapest query the provider accepts and stores the outcome in `lastError`. A provider that refuses the key answers 200 with `ok: false`: that is a valid answer to \"test this\", not a Memchats failure.","operationId":"testConnection","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"`{ ok: true }`, or `{ ok: false, error }`"},"403":{"description":"Connections require the Pro or Empresa plan"},"404":{"description":"Not found"},"503":{"description":"The server has no CONNECTIONS_SECRET_KEY"}}}},"/api/v1/devices":{"post":{"summary":"Register a device for push notifications","operationId":"registerDevice","responses":{"200":{"description":"Registered"}}},"delete":{"summary":"Unregister a device","operationId":"unregisterDevice","responses":{"200":{"description":"Unregistered"}}}},"/api/v1/me/profile":{"get":{"summary":"Get the profile the user filled in during onboarding","operationId":"getProfile","responses":{"200":{"description":"Profile"}}}},"/api/v1/notifications":{"get":{"summary":"List notifications","description":"Two sources in one list, newest first: what the memory editor learned (`kind: \"memory_operation\"`) and the notices the product writes, the end of an import (`kind: \"memory_ready\"`, with `deep_link` to the conversation and `read`) and the daily dating reminder (`kind: \"dating_cooling\"`, no contact and no names by design, `deep_link: \"/app/dating\"`). Ids come from two tables, so a stable client key is the pair (kind, id).","operationId":"listNotifications","parameters":[{"name":"family","in":"query","description":"Relationship family: family, partner, dating, friends, work, professional, other. Omit or \"all\" for every contact.","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["all","family","partner","dating","friends","work","professional","other"]}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Up to twenty cards, newest first","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"notifications":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"integer"},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["memory_operation","memory_ready","dating_cooling"]},"tag":{"type":"string"},"tag_color":{"type":"string"},"contact_id":{"type":"integer","nullable":true},"contact_name":{"type":"string"},"title":{"type":"string"},"body":{"type":"string"},"time":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"deep_link":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"read":{"type":"boolean"}}}}}}}}}}}},"/api/v1/admin/queues":{"get":{"summary":"Job counts per background queue","description":"Operator only: an ADMIN_SECRET bearer token or a session on the admin allow-list. Read `pending` rather than `waiting`: embedding jobs carry a priority, so they live in the prioritized set and `waiting` reads 0 with hundreds of jobs queued.","operationId":"adminQueueCounts","responses":{"200":{"description":"Counts per queue"},"401":{"description":"Not an operator"},"503":{"description":"REDIS_URL not configured"}}}},"/api/v1/onboarding/next":{"get":{"summary":"Get the next unanswered onboarding question","description":"204 with no body when the profile has no questions left.","operationId":"nextOnboardingQuestion","responses":{"200":{"description":"The next question and the answered/total progress"},"204":{"description":"No questions left"}}}},"/api/v1/onboarding/answer":{"post":{"summary":"Answer an onboarding question","operationId":"answerOnboarding","responses":{"200":{"description":"Saved"}}}},"/api/v1/auth/signup":{"post":{"summary":"Create an account","description":"Does not require authentication.","operationId":"signup","security":[],"responses":{"201":{"description":"Created"},"409":{"description":"Email already in use"}}}},"/api/v1/auth/token":{"post":{"summary":"Exchange credentials for an API token","description":"Does not require authentication. grant_type is one of password, refresh_token, apple_identity_token (native Sign in with Apple) or authorization_code (the code returned to the mobile app by /api/v1/auth/authorize, with its PKCE code_verifier and the app redirect_uri). Optional offline: true (password and apple_identity_token) adds the offline_access scope, so the refresh token is an offline token that survives 30 days without use; refresh_token keeps the scope of the token it renews.","operationId":"issueToken","security":[],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Token"},"401":{"description":"Bad credentials"}}}},"/api/v1/auth/authorize":{"get":{"summary":"Start a Google or Apple sign-in from the mobile app","description":"Does not require authentication. Opened in the system browser; redirects (302) to Keycloak with kc_idp_hint for the provider and the app redirect URI. The code that comes back is exchanged at /api/v1/auth/token with grant_type authorization_code.","operationId":"authorizeWithProvider","security":[],"parameters":[{"name":"provider","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","enum":["google","apple"]}},{"name":"state","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","minLength":16,"maxLength":128}},{"name":"code_challenge","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","minLength":43,"maxLength":43}},{"name":"code_challenge_method","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","enum":["S256"]}},{"name":"offline","in":"query","required":false,"schema":{"type":"string","enum":["true"]},"description":"Ask for an offline refresh token (mobile app)."}],"responses":{"302":{"description":"Redirect to the identity provider"},"400":{"description":"Invalid request"},"404":{"description":"Provider not available on this server"}}}},"/api/v1/auth/providers":{"get":{"summary":"Identity providers available through the browser","description":"Does not require authentication. Lists the providers the apps can offer through the system browser (google, and apple when enabled).","operationId":"listBrowserProviders","security":[],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Available providers","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"browser":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","enum":["apple","google"]}}}}}}}}}},"/api/v1/me":{"get":{"summary":"Get account info","operationId":"getMe","responses":{"200":{"description":"Account information, plan, and usage stats","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object"}}}}}}},"/api/v1/contacts":{"post":{"summary":"Create a contact","description":"Subject to the plan contact limit. relationship_type is required: it drives the advisor tone and is the only way the user can tell their worlds apart. \"other\" is a valid answer.","operationId":"createContact","requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","required":["name","relationship_type"],"properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"display_name":{"type":"string"},"phone":{"type":"string"},"email":{"type":"string","format":"email"},"telegram_username":{"type":"string"},"instagram_username":{"type":"string"},"relationship_type":{"type":"string","enum":["partner","ex_partner","dating","want_to_meet","family","friend","acquaintance","work_colleague","work_boss","work_subordinate","cofounder","client","professional_service","lawyer","other"]},"context_note":{"type":"string","maxLength":2000}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Created"},"400":{"description":"Missing or unknown relationship_type (code: relationship_required)"},"402":{"description":"Plan contact limit reached"}}},"get":{"summary":"List contacts","operationId":"listContacts","parameters":[{"name":"includeDating","in":"query","description":"Dating contacts (relationship family dating, or with a dating profile) are left out by default for privacy: they live on their own screen. Send 1 to include them.","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["0","1"]}},{"name":"limit","in":"query","schema":{"type":"integer","default":50,"maximum":100}},{"name":"offset","in":"query","schema":{"type":"integer","default":0}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"List of contacts with memory level","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"contacts":{"type":"array"},"total":{"type":"integer"}}}}}}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/export":{"get":{"summary":"Export contact memory as downloadable JSON","operationId":"exportContactMemory","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Structured JSON export with contact info, memory, and recent messages. Intended for therapist or personal review.","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"export_info":{"type":"object","properties":{"generated_at":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"generated_by":{"type":"string"},"disclaimer":{"type":"string"},"contact_name":{"type":"string"}}},"contact":{"type":"object"},"memory":{"type":"object","nullable":true},"memory_version":{"type":"integer"},"recent_messages_sample":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object"}}}}}}},"401":{"description":"Unauthorized"},"404":{"description":"Contact not found"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/pre-call":{"get":{"summary":"Get pre-call summary for a contact","operationId":"getPreCallSummary","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Short summary to prepare a call/meeting","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"summary":{"type":"string"},"contact_name":{"type":"string"},"has_memory":{"type":"boolean"},"open_commitments":{"type":"integer"},"active_threads":{"type":"integer"}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Contact not found"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/knowledge/warm":{"post":{"summary":"Warm the external knowledge of a business contact","description":"Fire-and-forget hint sent when a contact is opened. Asks the user's connected products (MemoryFirst, TubExperto) the same question Alma will ask later, so the first answer is not paying for a cold start. Never an error when there is nothing to warm: it answers 200 with `warmed: false` and the reason. Rate-limited to one call per minute per contact.","operationId":"warmContactKnowledge","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Whether anything was warmed, and how long each provider took","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"warmed":{"type":"boolean"},"reason":{"type":"string","enum":["plan","not_business","no_context","too_soon","no_connection"],"description":"Only when `warmed` is false."},"providers":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"provider":{"type":"string","enum":["memoryfirst","tubexperto"]},"ms":{"type":"integer"},"ok":{"type":"boolean"},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["auth","timeout","network","server"]}}}}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Contact not found"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/health-score":{"get":{"summary":"Get relationship health score for a contact","operationId":"getConversationHealth","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Health score (0-100) calculated from commitments, emotional tone, and active threads","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"score":{"type":"integer","nullable":true,"minimum":0,"maximum":100},"label":{"type":"string","nullable":true,"enum":["excelente","buena","regular","necesita atención"]},"contact_name":{"type":"string"},"has_memory":{"type":"boolean"},"factors":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Contact not found"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/memory":{"get":{"summary":"Get contact memory","description":"While the initial sweep is running the sheet is returned as it stands, with `partial: true` and the live counter in `importing`. A half-built memory is useful and is labelled rather than hidden; the alternative was showing it as if it were finished.","operationId":"getContactMemory","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Full memory: traits, timeline, commitments, and the verdicts it adds up to, plus `partial` and `importing`","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"partial":{"type":"boolean","description":"True while the sweep is still running. Same fact as `importing !== null`."},"importing":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ImportingStatus"}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Contact not found"}}}},"/api/v1/imports/people":{"post":{"summary":"Import a person from screenshots (dating profile or chat) in one request","description":"Multipart. Returns 202 at once; the server reads every image in parallel, classifies each one (dating profile / chat / other), extracts the name, saves the contact and prepares the first proposal. Poll GET /api/v1/imports/people/{importId}. The public demo is allowed: at most 6 images, 3 imports per session, and the proposal spends one of its five generations.","operationId":"createPeopleImport","parameters":[{"name":"X-Client-Prepare-Ms","in":"header","required":false,"schema":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":600000},"description":"Optional. Whole ms from \"Import\" pressed to the upload starting (shrinking, re-encoding). Kept in the timing record only when valid; ignored otherwise."},{"name":"X-Client-Platform","in":"header","required":false,"schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[a-z0-9._-]{1,32}$"},"description":"Optional. The client and its version, e.g. `web`, `ios-0.2.6`, `android-0.2.6`. Ignored when it does not match."}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"multipart/form-data":{"schema":{"type":"object","required":["kind","files"],"properties":{"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["dating","conversation"]},"family":{"type":"string","enum":["partner","family","friends","work","professional","other"],"description":"Conversation only; optional."},"type":{"type":"string","description":"Optional concrete relationship type within the family."},"files":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","format":"binary"},"minItems":1,"maxItems":30,"description":"Repeat the field once per image (`files[]` also accepted)."}}}}}},"responses":{"202":{"description":"Started","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PeopleImportStatus"}}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid kind, no images or too many (code too_many_images, max)"},"402":{"description":"Plan limit (code tier_limit_exceeded, with `limit`)"},"413":{"description":"An image or the whole import is too large"},"415":{"description":"Not an image"},"429":{"description":"Demo import limit (code demo_import_limit), or the plan monthly screenshots: dating imports spend the dating meter (code dating_quota_exceeded) and conversation imports their own (code conversation_quota_exceeded; Free 60, Plus 300, Pro and Empresa 800), both with `limit`, `used`, `remaining`, `resetsAt`. An import that does not fit is refused whole; admins and demo sessions are not held to it"}}}},"/api/v1/imports/people/{importId}":{"get":{"summary":"Status of a people import","description":"Cheap: one Redis read. Another user's import answers 404 like a missing one.","operationId":"getPeopleImport","parameters":[{"name":"importId","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Status","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PeopleImportStatus"}}}},"404":{"description":"Import not found"}}},"delete":{"summary":"Discard a people import","description":"The \"Discard\" of the \"import in progress\" card. `needs_name` and `failed`: deleted for good (the R2 crops and originals no row cites, then the state). `done`: only hides the card, the saved person is untouched. `processing`: 409, a running import cannot be stopped from here (a dead one is first marked `interrupted` and can then be discarded). Another user's import answers 404 like a missing one.","operationId":"discardPeopleImport","parameters":[{"name":"importId","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Discarded; the final status","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PeopleImportStatus"}}}},"404":{"description":"Import not found"},"409":{"description":"Still processing, or a name is being saved at the same moment"}}}},"/api/v1/imports/people/{importId}/name":{"post":{"summary":"Answer \"¿Cómo se llama?\" and finish the import","description":"Only valid while status is needs_name. Resumes from what was already read and answers with the full status, waiting for the import to finish (up to 45 s) so the client can land at once.","operationId":"namePeopleImport","parameters":[{"name":"importId","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","required":["name"],"properties":{"name":{"type":"string","maxLength":120}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Status after resuming","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/PeopleImportStatus"}}}},"400":{"description":"name is required"},"404":{"description":"Import not found"},"409":{"description":"Not waiting for a name (already resumed or finished); body carries the current status"}}}},"/api/v1/imports/people/{importId}/client-timing":{"post":{"summary":"Report how long the import took on the client","description":"Optional, sent once the client lands on the result: the whole wait from \"Import\" pressed to the person on screen, and how long the app or tab was in the background meanwhile (iOS suspends polling there). Numbers only, joined to the import's timing record. Owner only; another user's import answers 404 like a missing one. Idempotent: sending it again overwrites with the same values.","operationId":"reportPeopleImportClientTiming","parameters":[{"name":"importId","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","required":["clientTotalMs"],"properties":{"clientTotalMs":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":600000},"backgroundedMs":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":600000,"description":"Defaults to 0; capped at clientTotalMs."}}}}}},"responses":{"204":{"description":"Kept"},"400":{"description":"A value is missing, not a whole number, or out of range"},"404":{"description":"Import not found"}}}},"/api/v1/imports/people/{importId}/notify":{"post":{"summary":"Ask for a push when the import stops","description":"`{ \"enabled\": true }` when the app goes to the background (or the tab is hidden) while the import is processing: when it stops (done, needs a name, or failed) the account gets ONE push through the existing notification sender, without names. `{ \"enabled\": false }` when the client comes back clears it. On an import that already stopped it does nothing. Owner only; idempotent.","operationId":"notifyPeopleImport","parameters":[{"name":"importId","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","format":"uuid"}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","required":["enabled"],"properties":{"enabled":{"type":"boolean"}}}}}},"responses":{"204":{"description":"Saved"},"400":{"description":"`enabled` is not a boolean"},"404":{"description":"Import not found"}}}},"/api/v1/imports/active":{"get":{"summary":"Every memory sweep running right now for this account","description":"The counter used to live only under its contact, so leaving the import screen lost it. This answers the inverse question — what is running for me — from a Redis set the sweep maintains, never a key scan. Empty array when nothing is running, and never a 5xx: a progress bar cannot be the reason a screen breaks. Demo sessions may read it.","operationId":"listActiveImports","responses":{"200":{"description":"The live sweeps, with the contact each one belongs to","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"imports":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"contactId":{"type":"integer"},"contactName":{"type":"string"},"processed":{"type":"integer"},"total":{"type":"integer"},"passIndex":{"type":"integer"},"passCount":{"type":"integer"},"phase":{"type":"string","enum":["reading","writing"]},"passRange":{"type":"object","nullable":true,"properties":{"fromMessageId":{"type":"integer"},"toMessageId":{"type":"integer"},"fromAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"toAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"messages":{"type":"integer"}}},"sweepWindow":{"type":"integer","nullable":true,"description":"The plan's window when the sweep has one; null means the whole history."},"startedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"updatedAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"}}}}}}}}},"401":{"description":"No session"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/memory/regenerate":{"post":{"summary":"Read the whole history again, from the beginning","description":"Replaces the contact's memory sheet with one distilled from every message, ignoring the watermark and any plan window. Takes minutes; the messages themselves are untouched. Plus and above: on Free the sweep would be bounded to the same 2,000 most recent messages the sheet already has.","operationId":"regenerateContactMemory","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The resweep is queued","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"ok":{"type":"boolean"},"contact_id":{"type":"integer"},"status":{"type":"string","enum":["queued"]}}}}}},"402":{"description":"Plus or above required (code: plan_required)"},"404":{"description":"Contact not found"},"429":{"description":"A sweep is already running for this contact (code: sweep_running)"},"503":{"description":"The memory queue is not available"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/import-progress":{"get":{"summary":"How far the initial memory sweep has got","description":"Poll while an import is in flight. 204 means nothing is running, which is different from 0%.","operationId":"getImportProgress","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Messages read so far, pass counter, signal level and the last observations","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"contact_id":{"type":"integer"},"processed":{"type":"integer"},"total":{"type":"integer"},"pass_index":{"type":"integer"},"pass_count":{"type":"integer"},"phase":{"type":"string","enum":["reading","writing"],"description":"Reading a stretch of conversation, or filing what was found in it. A pass takes about a minute, so both are published: without this the counter stands still for that minute, which reads as a dead import."},"pass_range":{"type":"object","description":"The stretch the current pass covers. Absent on a counter written before phases existed.","properties":{"from_message_id":{"type":"integer"},"to_message_id":{"type":"integer"},"from_at":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"to_at":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"messages":{"type":"integer"}}},"sweep_window":{"type":"integer","description":"The plan's window, when the sweep has one. Absent means the whole history."},"history_total":{"type":"integer","description":"The whole history behind that window."},"signal":{"type":"string","enum":["excellent","good","starter"]},"latest_observations":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"started_at":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"updated_at":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"Last heartbeat: what tells a working sweep from one whose worker died."}}}}}},"204":{"description":"No import running for this contact"},"404":{"description":"Contact not found"}}}},"/api/v1/conversations":{"get":{"summary":"List conversations","operationId":"listConversations","parameters":[{"name":"contact_id","in":"query","schema":{"type":"integer"}},{"name":"family","in":"query","description":"Relationship family: family, partner, dating, friends, work, professional, other. Omit or \"all\" for every contact.","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["all","family","partner","dating","friends","work","professional","other"]}},{"name":"includeDating","in":"query","description":"Dating contacts (relationship family dating, or with a dating profile) are left out by default for privacy: they live on their own screen. Send 1 to include them. Asking for family=dating or for one contact_id shows them without this flag.","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["0","1"]}},{"name":"limit","in":"query","schema":{"type":"integer","default":50,"maximum":100}},{"name":"offset","in":"query","schema":{"type":"integer","default":0}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"List of conversations ordered by last message","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"conversations":{"type":"array"},"total":{"type":"integer"}}}}}}}}},"/api/v1/conversations/{id}/messages":{"post":{"summary":"Send a message and get Alma's reply","description":"Consumes one LLM query from the weekly plan quota.","operationId":"sendMessage","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"The reply"},"429":{"description":"Weekly Alma analysis quota exhausted, with `resetsAt`"}}},"get":{"summary":"Get messages from a conversation","operationId":"getMessages","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}},{"name":"limit","in":"query","schema":{"type":"integer","default":50,"maximum":200}},{"name":"offset","in":"query","schema":{"type":"integer","default":0}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Messages ordered chronologically","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"messages":{"type":"array"}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Conversation not found"}}}},"/api/v1/conversations/{id}/read":{"post":{"summary":"Mark a conversation as read up to a message","description":"The backup way out of \"unread\": the reader reached the end of the history. The main one needs no call at all, because the server marks it when Alma summarises what is new. Send the id of the last message the client actually rendered; without it the mark moves to the contact's latest message.","operationId":"markConversationRead","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"requestBody":{"required":false,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"message_id":{"type":"integer"}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"The mark, after moving it (it only ever moves forward)"},"404":{"description":"Conversation not found"}}}},"/api/v1/search":{"get":{"summary":"Full-text search in messages","operationId":"searchMessages","parameters":[{"name":"q","in":"query","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","minLength":2}},{"name":"contact_id","in":"query","schema":{"type":"integer"}},{"name":"family","in":"query","description":"Relationship family: family, partner, dating, friends, work, professional, other. Omit or \"all\" for every contact.","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["all","family","partner","dating","friends","work","professional","other"]}},{"name":"includeDating","in":"query","description":"Dating contacts (relationship family dating, or with a dating profile) are left out by default for privacy: they live on their own screen. Send 1 to include them. Asking for family=dating or for one contact_id shows them without this flag.","schema":{"type":"string","enum":["0","1"]}},{"name":"limit","in":"query","schema":{"type":"integer","default":20,"maximum":100}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Ranked search results","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"results":{"type":"array"},"total":{"type":"integer"}}}}}}}}},"/api/v1/me/wrapped":{"get":{"summary":"Monthly Wrapped: stats summary for a given month","operationId":"getWrapped","parameters":[{"name":"month","in":"query","description":"Month in YYYY-MM format. Defaults to the last 30 days.","schema":{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\d{4}-\\d{2}$","example":"2026-04"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Monthly communication stats including top contact, active contacts, memories built, and commitment tracking","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"month":{"type":"string","example":"2026-04"},"top_contact":{"type":"object","nullable":true,"properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"messages":{"type":"integer"}}},"total_messages":{"type":"integer"},"total_contacts_active":{"type":"integer"},"new_memories_built":{"type":"integer"},"sentiment_summary":{"type":"string","enum":["positivo","neutro","negativo"]},"top_pattern":{"type":"string","nullable":true},"most_active_channel":{"type":"string"},"commitment_stats":{"type":"object","properties":{"created":{"type":"integer"},"fulfilled":{"type":"integer"},"broken":{"type":"integer"}}}}}}}},"401":{"description":"Unauthorized"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/analyze-patterns":{"post":{"summary":"Read the behaviour patterns detected on both sides of a conversation","operationId":"analyzePatterns","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"Pattern analysis result with risk level and detected patterns","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"contact_name":{"type":"string"},"analyzed_messages":{"type":"integer"},"disclaimer":{"type":"string","description":"Localised by account language"},"patterns_detected":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"integer","description":"Pattern id, for POST /patterns/{patternId}/dismiss"},"type":{"type":"string","description":"Pattern key from the catalogue"},"subject":{"type":"string","enum":["user","contact"],"description":"Whose behaviour this is. Detection is bidirectional."},"subject_label":{"type":"string","description":"The contact's name, or the second person for the user"},"severity":{"type":"string","enum":["info","caution","alert"]},"severity_label":{"type":"string","description":"Localised severity"},"title":{"type":"string","description":"Localised by account language"},"description":{"type":"string"},"occurrences":{"type":"integer"},"evidence_message_ids":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"integer"}},"dismissable":{"type":"boolean"},"first_detected":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"},"last_confirmed":{"type":"string","format":"date-time"}}}},"risk_level":{"type":"string","enum":["insufficient","low","moderate","high"]},"risk_level_label":{"type":"string","description":"Localised risk level"},"summary":{"type":"string","description":"Localised by account language"}}}}}},"404":{"description":"Contact not found"},"422":{"description":"No conversations found or insufficient messages"}}}},"/api/v1/contacts/{id}/compatibility/{id2}":{"get":{"summary":"Compatibility Snapshot between two contacts","operationId":"getCompatibility","parameters":[{"name":"id","in":"path","required":true,"description":"First contact ID","schema":{"type":"integer"}},{"name":"id2","in":"path","required":true,"description":"Second contact ID","schema":{"type":"integer"}}],"responses":{"200":{"description":"AI-generated compatibility analysis between two contacts based on their memory profiles","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"contact_1":{"type":"string"},"contact_2":{"type":"string"},"score":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":100},"label":{"type":"string","enum":["Alta compatibilidad","Buena compatibilidad","Compatibilidad moderada","Poca compatibilidad"]},"summary":{"type":"string"},"shared_traits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"tension_points":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Invalid contact ids or same contact compared with itself"},"404":{"description":"One or both contacts not found"},"422":{"description":"Insufficient memory for one or both contacts"}}}},"/api/v1/advisors":{"get":{"summary":"List the counsellor and the areas she answers with","description":"One entry, Alma, plus `verticals`: the four areas (legal, relaciones, conocer, negocio). The five character advisors this used to list have been retired, and no area is sold separately.","operationId":"listAdvisors","responses":{"200":{"description":"Alma, and the four areas she answers with","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object"}}}}}}},"/api/v1/advisors/{slug}/ask":{"post":{"summary":"Ask Alma about a contact, choosing the area","description":"There is one counsellor, Alma. The slug says which area she answers with: `alma` (and `memchats`) let her detect it from who the contact is and what the exchange is about, while `legal`, `relaciones`, `conocer` and `negocio` set it explicitly. The five retired advisor slugs are kept for backwards compatibility with existing API tokens and the published MCP server, and map onto the areas: `lexiel` to legal, `amoriel` and `pactiel` to relaciones, `cupiel` to conocer, `proxiel` to negocio. No area depends on the plan: all four are available on every plan, Free included. Same pipeline and same quota as POST /api/v1/alma/respond (consumes one LLM query from the plan quota), returned in the flat `{ answer, advisor, contact_id }` shape older clients read.","operationId":"askAdvisor","parameters":[{"name":"slug","in":"path","required":true,"schema":{"type":"string","enum":["alma","relaciones","conocer","negocio","legal","memchats","lexiel","amoriel","cupiel","proxiel","pactiel"]}}],"requestBody":{"required":true,"content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","required":["contact_id","question"],"properties":{"contact_id":{"type":"integer"},"question":{"type":"string","maxLength":2000}}}}}},"responses":{"200":{"description":"Alma's answer, flattened into a single text","content":{"application/json":{"schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"answer":{"type":"string"},"advisor":{"type":"string"},"contact_id":{"type":"integer"}}}}}},"400":{"description":"Malformed body, or a question over 2000 characters"},"404":{"description":"Contact not found"},"429":{"description":"Weekly Alma analysis quota exhausted, with `resetsAt`"}}}}}}